# Implement — etude-9uf.4: Shrink the completeness audit

## What shipped

8 files, **+314 / −2404**. Net −2090.

| File | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| `scripts/dogfood-completeness-audit.sh` | 902 | **148** |
| `scripts/dogfood-completeness-audit_test.sh` | 1579 | **226** |
| total | 2481 | 374 |

Exact counts by `grep -c ''`, as the plan required rather than "about 60". The
acceptance's original "~60 lines" was written for two ratchets; this ships four
checks plus a bypass report, and roughly 40 of the 148 are the header explaining
why (a) and (b) survive — which is the record of a premise the plan gate
overturned, so it earns its lines.

## The checks

| Check | Severity | What it catches |
|---|---|---|
| (a) run ref present | hard | a bead closed with no run at all |
| (b) run has gates | hard | a run captured but never gated |
| (d) refs pushed | hard | a local ref absent from or diverged from origin |
| (c) retro cadence | **WARN** | 3+ active beads uncovered by a cadence retro |

Dropped: (e) docs drift (duplicates `make docs-check` / `make docs-reality`,
which the verify gate already runs as deterministic checks), (f) cadence-sidecar,
(g) retro subject consistency, and the `--bead` / `--since` / `--json` /
`--quiet` flags. Verified before dropping: no non-test caller of any of the four
flags exists; `--bead`'s only caller was `scripts/dogfood-close.sh`, deleted in
bead `.3`.

**(a) and (b) survive against the bead as originally filed.** The bead said they
"become structurally true once `etude gate` is the only way to advance a phase".
Nothing makes `etude gate` the only way — no hook, CLI path or `bd close` guard
requires a run ref or a gate. Both plan-gate seats upheld that, and the bead text
and acceptance were updated in this bead accordingly.

**The allowlist stays**, against the bead's "it goes with the checks it served".
It also feeds check (c)'s denominator. Measured during planning: emptying it
moves (c)'s uncovered count from 1 to exactly its threshold of 3. The one-line
bypass report stays with it, because the allowlist header promises exemptions
"remain visible + auditable" — dropping the report would have made 3 of 9
in-scope beads exempt AND invisible, and turned that header into a claim about
behavior that no longer exists.

## The contract the pre-push hook depends on

Preserved exactly: `0` clean, `1` hard gaps, `2` usage/environment error. The
hook fails CLOSED on 2, and `scripts/pre-push_test.sh` (extracted in `.3`) drives
that path — B9 covers a missing audit script, B10 covers audit-exit-2. **20/20
still green.** `--last <N>` still works; both the hook and `make dogfood-audit`
pass `--last 9`.

