### Negative controls

Chosen so each one's failure is observable, after `.3` taught that a control
targeting a masked branch proves nothing. All run and reverted:

| Control | Result |
|---|---|
| plant a local `refs/etude/runs/*` absent from origin | exit 1, `[unpushed-ref]` names it |
| same tree with no gap | exit 0 — so the control above is attributable, not a script that always fails |
| closed bead with no run ref (isolated fixture) | exit 1, `[missing-run]` |
| run ref whose manifest has zero gates | exit 1, `[gateless-run]` — **the case the first draft of the plan would have made undetectable** |
| 3 uncovered beads, hard checks clean | **exit 0** with `WARN [cadence-overdue]` — pins that (c) warns and never fails |
| unknown flag | exit 2, so the hook's fail-closed branch still receives 2 |

All six are also encoded as cases in the new test, so they are permanent rather
than one-off.

